{
  "path": "/charge_usage/list/1",
  "method": "get",
  "operation": {
    "summary": "Get All Credit Usage Amount",
    "deprecated": false,
    "description": "Read operation. Retrieve all required pages before reporting complete totals. Returns a paginated list of charge usage records. A charge usage links a credit charge to a credit usage and stores the amount consumed.\n\nThis is a v2 native-entity endpoint served from the `/v2/api/entity` base and authenticated with a Bearer token.\n\nThe trailing path segment (`1`) is the **data level** — how deeply related records are loaded — not a page number. `/charge_usage/list` and `/charge_usage/list/1` return the same result. Pagination is controlled by the `page` and `per_page` query parameters.\n\n| Parameter | Purpose |\n|---|---|\n| `page` | Page number (default `1`). |\n| `per_page` | Items per page (default `20`). |\n| `filter[<field>][<operator>]` | Filter rows by a field's value, e.g. `filter[credit_usage_id][equal]=5`. |\n| `sort[<field>]` | Sort by a field, `asc` or `desc`, e.g. `sort[amount]=desc`. |\n\n**Filterable fields.** The fields intended for filtering:\n\n| Field | Type | Example |\n|---|---|---|\n| `credit_charge_id` | integer (credit charge) | `filter[credit_charge_id][equal]=12` |\n| `credit_usage_id` | integer (credit usage) | `filter[credit_usage_id][equal]=5` |\n| `amount` | number | `filter[amount][greater_than]=10` |\n\nThe list will in fact filter and sort on any existing column, not only the fields above. When no `sort` is given the default ordering is newest first (`id` descending).\n\nEach item in `data` is a flat charge-usage record.",
    "tags": [
      "Endpoints/Points & Credits/Credit Usage"
    ],
    "parameters": [
      {
        "name": "page",
        "in": "query",
        "description": "Page number. Defaults to `1`.",
        "required": false,
        "schema": {
          "type": "integer"
        }
      },
      {
        "name": "per_page",
        "in": "query",
        "description": "Items per page. Defaults to `20`.",
        "required": false,
        "schema": {
          "type": "integer"
        }
      },
      {
        "name": "filter[<field>][<operator>]",
        "in": "query",
        "description": "Filter rows by a field's value, e.g. `filter[credit_usage_id][equal]=5`. Filterable fields: `credit_charge_id`, `credit_usage_id`, `amount` (the API also accepts any other existing column).",
        "required": false,
        "schema": {
          "type": "string"
        }
      },
      {
        "name": "sort[<field>]",
        "in": "query",
        "description": "Sort by a field, `asc` or `desc`, e.g. `sort[id]=desc`. Default ordering is `id` descending.",
        "required": false,
